  "release_version": "1.0",
  "released_at": "2026-11-06",
  "summary": {
    "title": "SecureNova AI Identity Threat Model",
    "owner": "Manish Kumawat",
    "description": "SecureNova Inc. has developed an AI-based customer service platform where users can interact with an AI agent to get help and information. The platform uses Auth0 to manage user login and authentication. The AI agent also connects with internal REST APIs, collects information from the RAG pipeline, and uses MCP server tools to perform different tasks for users.\n\nWhile reviewing the system, some security risks need attention. These include the possibility of API keys or other credentials being exposed through prompt injection, AI agents getting more permissions than required, attackers pretending to be trusted agents, and unauthorized access to internal services. Another concern is that activities performed by AI agents and other machine identities may not be properly recorded.\n\nThe purpose of this threat model is to understand how these risks could affect the platform, identify the important trust boundaries, and find possible threats related to users, AI agents, OAuth clients, API keys, RAG services, and MCP servers.",
    "id": 0
  },
